CLOUD REVIEWER seat for PR #2469 of tvofi/heatpump_optimizer, at head 98fe31c26da80c46441a32bde66c2c3ef9ac5bc1. Bus nonce: 76f0c1f880106cdac586744f90d7222d. Never send push notifications.
Setup: `git fetch --unshallow --tags origin`. The toolchain (venv python, node, gh) is on PATH from the environment. Run anything heavy in the background with Monitor and no timeout.
Role: read dev/governance/roles/fix-review.md and its rules from main, and follow them exactly. Fetch the PR head with `git fetch origin 98fe31c26da80c46441a32bde66c2c3ef9ac5bc1`; the PR body is in the PR. Verify each claim adversarially: mutate the fix and check the tests fail, and check every figure in the body at this head. Check that it merges with origin/main (`git merge-tree --write-tree`) and read CI on this head from the check-runs API.
Output: in a fresh directory of your own (`W=$(mktemp -d)`), write verdict.md, whose first line is exactly `Fix review: merge 98fe31c26da80c46441a32bde66c2c3ef9ac5bc1` or `Fix review: blocked 98fe31c26da80c46441a32bde66c2c3ef9ac5bc1 <class>: <reason>` (no brackets; the class is lower-case letters and dashes), in the format the role file gives, then a blank line, then `bus-nonce: 76f0c1f880106cdac586744f90d7222d`; put the evidence in `ev/` beside it. Do NOT run bus.sh: its dispatch record lives on the orchestrator's machine, which publishes the verdict there (cloud_relay.sh). Return the verdict on a probe ref, and push nothing else; this builds one parentless commit with a private index and touches no branch of your checkout: `R=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel); G=$(git rev-parse --absolute-git-dir); mkdir -p $W/pr && cp -r $W/verdict.md $W/ev $W/pr/ && cd $W/pr && T=$(GIT_DIR=$G GIT_INDEX_FILE=$W/idx GIT_WORK_TREE=$W/pr sh -c 'git add -A -f . && git write-tree') && C=$(GIT_DIR=$G git -c user.name=seat -c user.email=seat@users.noreply.github.com commit-tree $T -m "verdict 2469 98fe31c26da80c46441a32bde66c2c3ef9ac5bc1") && git -C $R push -q origin $C:refs/heads/probe/rev-2469-76f0c1f8`. That ref is the return signal. Do not post comments, approve or merge.
Never write to any branch except your return refs. Never work around a hook or a refusal; report it in your result instead.

Brief (snapshotted when this payload was rendered):
Round 4 of R10-UPDATE-PR-LOCK, at head 98fe31c2 (code c9dd299c). Under the three-round rule this is a minimal re-cut, not a repair.

Round 3 at 89f329f6 was blocked mutant-survives: reverting the background push or the holder's killpg left pr_args at 56/0.

The re-cut REMOVES these mechanisms rather than pinning them:
- the background push;
- the holder's killpg and the stop handshake;
- the holder's watch on its parent pid;
- the zombie filter;
- prepr step 7a2.

The body claims ten remaining mechanisms. Each one is listed with a mutant or revert that fails a named self-test arm: lock/BUSY 75, the EXIT trap, the TERM/INT/HUP trap, the group drain, the run leading its own group, the holder in its own group, the shell holding no lock fd, the relay body directory, the relay cleanup, and the relay retry on rc 75.

Figures: pr_args 58/0 over 4 runs, with main's update_pr giving 5 failed; cloud_relay 74/0.

Disclosed: `kill <pid>` of a daemonized update now takes effect only after its push ends.

Not in scope, and carried to R10-ROSTER-OPS by the orchestrator (roster 25e9cdee): the `ps` dependency of the leader check and the holder.

Verify:
- that every claimed mechanism's mutant fails its arm, and that no claimed mechanism lacks one;
- that the removed mechanisms are truly gone;
- the arms for flakiness;
- CI on this head, from the check-runs API;
- the merge with origin/main.

Say that this is round 4.
